  "description": "NEWCEZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C212 H294 Co8 N8 O54 Sm6,5(H2 O1),C3 H7 N1 O1. From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm3 (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Sm1A (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Sm2A (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm3A (Sm) has 8 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co3A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4A (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 26 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.215-4.946 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 80.72-160.48°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C215H311Sm6Co8N9O60. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Sm(III), Co(II).",
